# What never enters the image (phase 7 row 7.21).
#
# Two reasons, and the second is the important one: build speed, and the fact
# that a distributed image must carry no business's data. A real tenant is one
# company's vendor list, account names, paths and host wiring; the image ships
# the engine, the demo and the archetype templates, and `engine init` renders
# a tenant onto the volume at first boot.

# Every tenant folder but the two that ship: never in the product image, even
# one a developer has checked out beside the engine.
tenants/*
!tenants/demo/
!tenants/_templates/

# State that belongs to a host, not to an image.
.ledger/
.auditor/
demo-data/
*-data/
data/

# The checkout's own machinery. .git matters twice: it is large, and an image
# that carried it would let run-preflight.sh think it had a checkout to pull.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.venv/
.claude/

# Build and test leftovers.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
tests/
htmlcov/
.coverage
